 "title": "Every line of a knot sphere carries the forced dissonance equally often",
 "subject": "How the least-dissonance states of a Kasteleyn knot sphere distribute their one violated line",
 "conclusion": "On every simplicial two-coloured sphere triangulation with Kasteleyn signs, each line is the only violated line of exactly 2N(T) states with no over-agreeing face, where N(T)^2 = det(BB^T)/(n0n1 + n1n2 + n2n0) for the line-vertex matrix B and the class sizes n_i of the vertex 3-colouring. Two even faces of different colours never allow fewer consistent states than two adjacent ones.",
